## Review: Runtime Metrics Exposure

### Root Cause Analysis

The metrics are being tracked internally in `MetricsTracker` and persisted to disk via `persistSession()`, but **they are not exposed to the client via the protocol**. The `ServerMessage` union in the protocol has no metrics message type, and the client has no mechanism to receive real-time metrics updates.

### Protocol-First Fix Required

The smallest safe change is to add a metrics message type to the protocol and expose the current metrics state to connected clients.

### Files to Change

#### 1. `packages/protocol/src/messages.ts`

Add a new message type for metrics:

```typescript
export type ServerMessage =
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "session.state";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "world.snapshot";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "agent.turn";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "agent.action";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "agent.feed";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "build.result";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "error";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "runtime.metrics";
      payload: {
        tick: number;
        queuedActions: number;
        invalidOutputCount: number;
        actionAppliedCount: number;
        actionRejectedCount: number;
        turnsTotal: number;
      };
    };
```

Also add the metrics schema to `clientMessageSchema` (or `serverMessageSchema` if needed for bidirectional).

#### 2. `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts`

Add a method to send metrics and call it periodically:

```typescript
private sendMetrics(): void {
  if (!this.metrics) return;
  this.emitMessage({
    version: PROTOCOL_VERSION,
    type: "runtime.metrics",
    payload: {
      tick: this.simulation?.getState().tick ?? 0,
      queuedActions: this.totalQueuedActions(),
      invalidOutputCount: this.metrics.metrics.invalidOutputCount,
      actionAppliedCount: this.metrics.metrics.actionAppliedCount,
      actionRejectedCount: this.metrics.metrics.actionRejectedCount,
      turnsTotal: this.metrics.metrics.turnsTotal,
    }
  });
}
```

Update `startTimers()` to include metrics sending:

```typescript
this.persistTimer = setInterval(() => {
  void this.persistSession();
}, 2000);

this.metricsTimer = setInterval(() => {
  this.sendMetrics();
}, 1000); // Send metrics every second
```

Update `stopTimers()`:

```typescript
private stopTimers(): void {
  if (this.tickTimer) {
    clearInterval(this.tickTimer);
    this.tickTimer = null;
  }
  if (this.schedulerTimer) {
    clearInterval(this.schedulerTimer);
    this.schedulerTimer = null;
  }
  if (this.persistTimer) {
    clearInterval(this.persistTimer);
    this.persistTimer = null;
  }
  if (this.metricsTimer) {
    clearInterval(this.metricsTimer);
    this.metricsTimer = null;
  }
}
```

#### 3. `apps/game-client/src/App.tsx`

Listen for metrics messages:

```typescript
ws.onmessage = (event) => {
  const message = JSON.parse(event.data as string) as ServerMessage;

  switch (message.type) {
    case "session.state":
      // ... existing state handling
      return;
    case "world.snapshot":
      // ... existing snapshot handling
      return;
    case "runtime.metrics": {
      setMetrics({
        tick: message.payload.tick,
        queuedActions: message.payload.queuedActions,
        invalidOutputCount: message.payload.invalidOutputCount,
        actionAppliedCount: message.payload.actionAppliedCount,
        actionRejectedCount: message.payload.actionRejectedCount,
        turnsTotal: message.payload.turnsTotal,
      });
      return;
    }
    // ... other cases
  }
};
```

Add state:

```typescript
const [metrics, setMetrics] = useState({
  tick: 0,
  queuedActions: 0,
  invalidOutputCount: 0,
  actionAppliedCount: 0,
  actionRejectedCount: 0,
  turnsTotal: 0,
});
```

Display in UI (add to topbar):

```tsx
<span className="pill">
  Metrics: {metrics.turnsTotal} turns, {metrics.actionAppliedCount} applied, {metrics.actionRejectedCount} rejected
</span>
```

### Regression Checks

1. Protocol schema validates: `ClientMessage` and `ServerMessage` unions must be exhaustive
2. Metrics timer cleanup: ensure `stopTimers()` clears all intervals including `metricsTimer`
3. Client compatibility: existing clients that don't handle `runtime.metrics` will ignore unknown types
4. Persistence: metrics are still persisted to disk via `persistSession()` - this change only adds real-time exposure

